# VRM animation playback — protected (do not regress)

**User-confirmed good state (2026-06-27).** Read `memory-bank/vrm-animation-protected-state.md` before editing Mixamo retarget, loot presets, Kimodo apply, or `AnimationManager` primary-target logic.

## Invariants

| Area | Rule |
|------|------|
| Primary mixer | When `primaryAnimationVrm` set → `_getActiveAnimationControls()` returns **VRM control only**; `_silenceOrphanFbxMixer()` stops orphan FBX mixer |
| Preset swap | `quickChange` + `weightIn=1` / `weightOut=0` when primary VRM; no cross-fade stacking |
| Kimodo | `setPrimaryAnimationVrm` + single clip + silence orphan FBX |
| VRM0 retarget | Standard axis flip for `metaVersion === '0'` on **all** bones (legs + shoulders + arms) |
| Shoulders | **Do not skip** `mixamorigLeftShoulder` / `mixamorigRightShoulder` on passthrough |
| Scene yaw | `withNeutralVrmSceneRootForRetarget` only during retarget sampling — restore after |
| Tracks | Normalized humanoid bone names; `vrmMixamoPlaybackGuard` not bypassed |

## Forbidden without explicit user request

- Disabling VRM0 quat/vector flip on passthrough uploads (causes buckled knees).
- Skipping shoulder tracks on passthrough (causes twisted arms).
- Running FBX reference mixer alongside primary VRM mixer (causes layering).
- Passthrough-only animation “shortcuts” in `loadMixamoAnimation.js` / `kimodoMotionLoader.js` without user approval.

## Protected files

`animationManager.js`, `loadMixamoAnimation.js`, `kimodoMotionLoader.js`, `viewportExpressionVrm.js`, `vrmMixamoPlaybackGuard.js`, `studioAnimations.js`

## Before merging

Re-test Sifr2 upload → Walking preset → Kimodo. Run animation regression tests listed in `memory-bank/vrm-animation-protected-state.md`.
